Subject: [PATCH] ufs: core: apply initial clock rates through OPP when configured

Do not set each clock to its maximum before the OPP core has applied the
required performance state. Acquire all clock handles first, then let the
existing OPP callback raise the initial rates after the required OPPs.
Keep the legacy frequency-table path unchanged. Track current rates in
the OPP callback so clock scaling and error recovery see the applied rate.

diff --git a/drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c b/drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c
--- a/drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c
@@ -1156,7 +1156,8 @@
 
 			trace_ufshcd_clk_scaling(hba,
 				(scaling_down ? "scaled down" : "scaled up"),
-				clki->name, hba->clk_scaling.target_freq, freq);
+				clki->name, clki->curr_freq, freq);
+			clki->curr_freq = freq;
 		}
 	}
 
@@ -9928,7 +9929,8 @@
 		if (!strcmp(clki->name, "ref_clk"))
 			ufshcd_parse_dev_ref_clk_freq(hba, clki->clk);
 
-		if (clki->max_freq) {
+		/* OPP core raises required performance states before clocks. */
+		if (clki->max_freq && !hba->use_pm_opp) {
 			ret = clk_set_rate(clki->clk, clki->max_freq);
 			if (ret) {
 				dev_err(hba->dev, "%s: %s clk set rate(%dHz) failed, %d\n",
